  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\(cauchy)::real.sequence]\nRefines: S ::= a(n_)\nspecifies: S is \\real.sequence\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: epsilon is \\real\n  where: epsilon \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n  then:\n  . exists: N is \\natural\n    suchThat:\n    . forAll: n, m is \\natural\n      where:\n      . N \\:natural.leq?:/ n\n      . N \\:natural.leq?:/ m\n      then: \\real.abs(a(n) \\.real.-./ a(m)) \\:real.less?:/ epsilon\nDocumented:\n. adjective: \"Cauchy\"\n. description: \"A sequence is Cauchy if its terms eventually stay arbitrarily\n                close to each other.\"\nId: \"3bf9fa3d-791d-4ebf-b585-68dbdb2755b1\"",
